# tests/rungselect/revdet_highbytes.rxt — [M6.6.2 wave 0, D70] the cells that
# make src/opt/revdet.c's `rd_node` GUARD OBSERVABLE.
#
# HAND-WRITTEN, unlike rungselect.rxt next door (which is generated by
# docs/design/rungselect_impl/make_corpus.py and must not be hand-edited).
# These cells are not a shape enumeration; they are a targeted detector for one
# measured hazard, so they are written and reviewed rather than produced.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. D70 moved `struct Ast`'s per-kind fields into a tagged
# union. `rd_node` — the reversal copy constructor — cleared A_REP's
# `revbody`/`possessive` on EVERY kind it copies; before the union those writes
# were dead for other kinds, after it they land through `u.rep` on whatever
# payload the node really owns. The arithmetic, measured: the union sits at
# offset +40 and `u.cls.bits` spans +40..+71, so
#
#     u.rep.possessive @ +49      -> class bitmap BYTE 9      -> 0x48-0x4F (H-O)
#     u.rep.revbody    @ +56..+63 -> class bitmap BYTES 16-23 -> 0x80-0xBF
#
# i.e. an unguarded clear ZEROES the reversed body's membership for `H`-`O` and
# for the 0x80-0xBF range. `rd_node` is now guarded on `n->k == A_REP`.
#
# WHAT WENT WRONG BEFORE THESE CELLS EXISTED, and the reason to keep them:
# exactly 44 corpus patterns took the reverse-deterministic rung, and EVERY ONE
# was spelled in lowercase ASCII — not one had a bit in either clobbered range.
# The wave's four-axis byte-identity gate therefore reported ZERO differences
# with the guard removed. The corpus could not express the bug. These cells
# close that: every pattern below takes the rung AND has class bits in one of
# the two ranges, so removing the guard now moves both this file and the gate.
#
# WHAT THE FAILURE LOOKS LIKE, so a future reader knows what to expect: under
# an unguarded build the reversed body's class tests compile to an ALL-ZERO
# `rx_class_bitmap[32]`, the backward walk can never take them, and the LAST
# ITERATION'S CAPTURES — the thing `Ast.u.rep.revbody` exists to recover — come
# back UNSET. `((H)|I){3}J` on "HHHJ" reports groups (-1,-1)(-1,-1) where both
# oracles give (2,3)(2,3). THE WHOLE-MATCH SPAN IS UNCHANGED IN EVERY CASE,
# which is why THE `g` LINES BELOW ARE THE WHOLE POINT: an `m`-only version of
# this file would pass under the bug and certify nothing. Permanent detector:
# mech row S121.
#
# EVERY PATTERN IS CAPTURE-BEARING, for tests/rungselect/CLAUDE.md's reason: a
# capture-free pattern routes to the DFA under the default engine choice and
# never reaches src/gen/emit_vm.c, so the rung would be structurally invisible.
#
# EVERY PATTERN TAKES THE RUNG, verified rather than assumed, by the same stamp
# run_rungselect_tests.sh asserts against: each compiles to an artifact whose
# `#define RX_VM_RUNGS` has PCREC_VM_RUNG_REVDET (0x8) set. Measured 0x8 for all
# seven at the commit that added this file.
#
# EVERY EXPECTATION WAS PRODUCED BY BOTH ORACLES AND AGREED — python3 `re` and
# libpcre2 (10.46, via ctypes), all 48 cells, 0 disagreements. No cell here is
# `# pcre2-only`: python expresses all of them, since a `\xHH` subject decodes
# to a codepoint 0..255 and str-mode `re` is then byte-exact over latin-1.

pattern ((H)|I){3}J
m "HHHJ" 0 4
g 1 2 3
g 2 2 3
m "HHIJ" 0 4
g 1 2 3
g 2 1 2
m "IIIJ" 0 4
g 1 2 3
g 2 -1 -1
m "IHIJ" 0 4
g 1 2 3
g 2 1 2
n "HIJ"
m "HHHHJ" 1 5
g 1 3 4
g 2 3 4
n "HHH"
n ""

pattern ((H)|b){0,4}c
m "c" 0 1
g 1 -1 -1
g 2 -1 -1
m "Hc" 0 2
g 1 0 1
g 2 0 1
m "HHc" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 1 2
m "bHc" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 1 2
m "Hbc" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 0 1
m "bbc" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 -1 -1
m "HHHHc" 0 5
g 1 3 4
g 2 3 4
m "HHHHHc" 1 6
g 1 4 5
g 2 4 5

pattern ((I)|J){2}K
m "IIK" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 1 2
m "IJK" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 0 1
m "JIK" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 1 2
m "JJK" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 -1 -1
n "IK"
m "IIIK" 1 4
g 1 2 3
g 2 2 3
n ""

pattern ((\x80)|\x81){3}\x82
m "\x80\x80\x80\x82" 0 4
g 1 2 3
g 2 2 3
m "\x80\x81\x80\x82" 0 4
g 1 2 3
g 2 2 3
m "\x81\x81\x81\x82" 0 4
g 1 2 3
g 2 -1 -1
n "\x80\x82"
m "\x81\x80\x81\x82" 0 4
g 1 2 3
g 2 1 2

pattern ((\x80)|b){0,4}c
m "c" 0 1
g 1 -1 -1
g 2 -1 -1
m "\x80c" 0 2
g 1 0 1
g 2 0 1
m "\x80\x80c" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 1 2
m "b\x80c" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 1 2
m "\x80bc" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 0 1
m "bbc" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 -1 -1
m "\x80\x80\x80\x80c" 0 5
g 1 3 4
g 2 3 4

pattern (([\x80-\x8f])|b){0,4}c
m "c" 0 1
g 1 -1 -1
g 2 -1 -1
m "\x80c" 0 2
g 1 0 1
g 2 0 1
m "\x8fc" 0 2
g 1 0 1
g 2 0 1
m "\x80\x8fc" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 1 2
m "b\x8fc" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 1 2
m "\x8fbc" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 0 1
m "\x90c" 1 2
g 1 -1 -1
g 2 -1 -1

pattern ((\xb0)|\xb1){2}\xb2
m "\xb0\xb0\xb2" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 1 2
m "\xb0\xb1\xb2" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 0 1
m "\xb1\xb1\xb2" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 -1 -1
m "\xb1\xb0\xb2" 0 3
g 1 1 2
g 2 1 2
n "\xb0\xb2"

